<title>COLOMBIA: U.S. Navy holds annual UNITAS exercise in Colombia.</title>
<headline>U.S. Navy holds annual UNITAS exercise in Colombia.</headline>
<dateline>BOGOTA 1996-11-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Four U.S. Navy vessels including a submarine arrived in Colombia's Caribbean coastal port of Cartagena on Friday for three days of joint manoeuvres.</p>
<p>Navies from Colombia, Venezuela, Brazil, Argentina, Chile, Paraguay, Uruguay, Peru and Ecuador are taking part in the wargames, called Operation UNITAS.</p>
<p>The operation has been held annually since 1959 and is designed to improve the working relationship among the U.S. and South American navies.</p>
</text>
